{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01APRxjJ1dHBAzbCND9As2h4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# ADR: Shared domain and optional worktree runtime\n2\t\n3\t## Status\n4\t\n5\tAccepted for the delivered scope — 2026-11-10 (proposed 2026-10-14, for B31/B33/B35). The\n6\toptional worktree runtime (B35) was delivered in three slices, each reviewed independently, and\n7\tthe last amendment below states what stands and where it departs from the decisions above:\n8\ta protected Unix-socket endpoint with identity and handshake, five hosted read checks with typed\n9\tresults, a resident memo of pure Git reads, and admission lanes with a measurement. Not adopted,\n10\tand needing a spec of their own before they are claimed: CPU quota and affinity, per-command\n11\tmemory and I/O limits, a named pipe for Windows, routing the checks to the runtime by default.\n12\tPreserve accepted ADRs for active-context discovery, scoped Git readers, obligations and the"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"9af0f974-85df-4706-9273-c29a58ad2827","timestamp":"2026-11-10T20:15:10.761Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-788625154/worktree/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md","content":"# ADR: Shared domain and optional worktree runtime\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted for the delivered scope — 2026-11-10 (proposed 2026-10-14, for B31/B33/B35). The\noptional worktree runtime (B35) was delivered in three slices, each reviewed independently, and\nthe last amendment below states what stands and where it departs from the decisions above:\na protected Unix-socket endpoint with identity and handshake, five hosted read checks with typed\nresults, a resident memo of pure Git reads, and admission lanes with a measurement. Not adopted,\nand needing a spec of their own before they are claimed: CPU quota and affinity, per-command\nmemory and I/O limits, a named pipe for Windows, routing the checks to the runtime by default.\nPreserve accepted ADRs for active-context discovery, scoped Git readers, obligations and the","numLines":12,"startLine":1,"totalLines":314}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01APRxjJ1dHBAzbCND9As2h4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
