{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgurvzkcYEg2FnhkLdwrL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"decision: approved\n\nI re-checked the milestone at 80b49143, including the round-7 fix to the resident Git memo key. The fix is correct, the two earlier low findings are still open as low follow-ups, and I found one new low finding: a stale word in the roadmap. Nothing blocks approval.\n\nMy profile only allows `git status|ls-files`. `pose validate` was refused in \"don't ask\" mode, so I ran none of the tests or plan tools myself. Everything below comes from the sealed evidence and from reading the code.\n\n**Round-7 fix (memo key holds the effective Git configuration)**\n- `effectiveGitConfig` (`governance_read_view_git.go:55-68`) hashes the output of `git config --list -z --includes`. It does this once per operation per root and caches the result in the operation's state.\n- `residentGitKey` (`resident_git_memo.go:62-87`) puts that hash in the key. If the configuration can't be read (`config == \"\"`), the read is not memoized.\n- The memo key covers the commit, the shallow file's content, the effective config and the exact arguments.\n- Replacement objects and graft files can't make a memoized answer stale. Every Git read runs with `--no-replace-objects`, `GIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS=1` and `GIT_GRAFT_FILE=/dev/null` (`git_snapshot_integrity.go:572-584`, `governance_read_view_git.go:619`).\n- `TestTheEffectiveGitConfigurationFollowsTheUsersConfigurationFile` (`resident_git_memo_test.go:120`) shows that a new operation picks up a change to the user's config, and that one operation keeps the hash it took. The key tests (`:60-67`) cover different configs and an unreadable one.\n- The caller's environment is still checked at the handshake (`runtime_host.go:42-44,93`).\n\n**Earlier findings**\n- **R3-N4: not fixed.** At `runtime_measure_test.go:280` the heavy check started next to the short queries still throws away its output and where it ran. T5 at `:378` still claims every hosted run printed the standalone output.\n- **R3-N5: not fixed.** `runtime_host.go:160-161` still adds to `busy` before the reply is written, while the connection is still counted in flight. One command can briefly count twice.\n\n**Criteria**\n- **Exit gate: passed.** The roadmap gate is at `pose-shared-runtime.md:77-81`. The departures are stated plainly in the ADR status (`adr…:5-11`) and the roadmap (`:69-75`):\n  - there is no file watcher; the memo is keyed by commit instead;\n  - \"receipt before retry\" is met by never rerunning a command that may have run;\n  - CPU and per-command limits are not delivered.\n\n  The sealed runtime-qos and optional-worktree-runtime integration runs pass.\n- **Integration: passed.** The three member slices fit together: endpoint and handshake, then hosted reads with the memo, then admission lanes. The sealed integration refs for all three pass.\n- **Membership: passed.** All three member specs have `status: done`, and the round-7 fix is part of this subject.\n- **Regression: passed.** `unit:pose-mcp/go/test`, `build:pose-mcp/go/build` and all the sealed integration and reachability refs pass.\n- **Residual risk: passed.** Everything not delivered is pushed to draft specs outside this roadmap. The open findings are all low-severity follow-ups.\n\n**New finding**\n- **N1 (low):** `.pose/roadmaps/pose-shared-runtime.md:37` still links the ADR as \"Proposed\", but the ADR status (`adr…:5`) is now \"Accepted for the delivered scope\". The implementer asked for no more roadmap edits during this review, so this is a follow-up.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"N1\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \".pose/roadmaps/pose-shared-runtime.md\", \"line\": 37, \"summary\": \"The roadmap still links the ADR as 'Proposed' while the ADR status (adr 2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md:5) now reads 'Accepted for the delivered scope'; stale status text.\", \"action\": \"Update the ADR link text at roadmap line 37 to Accepted at the next roadmap edit after this milestone's review\", \"owner\": \"Oseias Pereira\", \"review_by\": \"2026-12-10\"}\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"R3-N4\", \"status\": \"not-fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go:280 still runs `go func() { defer wg.Done(); runtimeRun(\\\"review-check\\\", spec) }()` discarding output and via, while T5 at :378 claims every hosted run matched standalone; low follow-up, unchanged since round 3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R3-N5\", \"status\": \"not-fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:160-161 still increments busy on deadline before the reply is written and the connection leaves inflight; transient double count remains; low follow-up, unchanged since round 3\"}\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Round-7 delta: resident_git_memo.go (key with shallow digest + effective config digest, unreadable config not memoized, LRU budget), governance_read_view_git.go:41-72 and :320-418 (per-operation config digest, memo get/put, purity gating on empty stderr), gitCommandContext env (no-replace-objects, null graft file), resident_git_memo_test.go (key and config tests). Re-read runtime_host.go hosted handler (orphaned/busy accounting, env digest), runtime_measure_test.go S5-S6/T1-T7, ADR status section, roadmap milestone block and exit gate, member spec statuses (all done), tracked measurement reports. Shell beyond git status/ls-files was refused, so tests and plan tools were not run by me; relied on sealed evidence.\"\n  ,\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"exit-gate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the exit gate (roadmap :77-81) against the ADR status (:5-11) and the roadmap delivery note (:69-75): handshake/endpoint/lifecycle/fallback are delivered; the departures (no watcher, memo keyed by commit; no rerun of a command that may have run; no CPU/per-command limits) are stated explicitly; the sealed runtime QoS and optional-runtime integration runs pass. Concluded that the gate has falsifiable evidence and the departures are disclosed.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"integration\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The three slices compose: endpoint/handshake, then hosted reads with the resident memo keyed by commit, shallow and effective config, then admission lanes. Sealed integration runs pass for all three (optional-worktree-runtime, resident-cache, runtime-qos).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"membership\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/resident-cache-integration\", \"rationale\": \"All three ordered member specs have status: done in .pose/specs; the round-7 memo-key fix is part of the sealed subject and is covered by the resident-cache integration and key tests.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"regression\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Module unit tests, build and every sealed integration/reachability ref for pose-mcp pass at this subject.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"residual-risk\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\", \"rationale\": \"Undelivered items (CPU quota/affinity, per-command limits, Windows pipe, default routing) are disposed to separate draft specs (ADR :9-11, roadmap :18-20); the remaining findings R3-N4, R3-N5 and N1 are low-severity follow-ups.\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"The reviewer profile refused shell; the sealed validate run of pose-mcp (unit, build, integration, reachability) passes.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose review-check milestone:pose-shared-runtime/optional-worktree-runtime\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review; it runs after the attestation.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose closeout-check milestone:pose-shared-runtime/optional-worktree-runtime\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review; it runs after the attestation.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose assess discover --component pose-mcp\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; the reviewer profile refused shell, so the code was reviewed by reading.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose assess tech-debt\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; the reviewer profile refused shell.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; the reviewer profile refused shell; the changed files were swept directly.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1134,"cache_read_input_tokens":47392,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1134},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"3495eb00-0437-4589-910c-63d53b870c4d","timestamp":"2026-11-10T20:16:01.692Z","request_id":"req_011CgurvzaD7StuAaS5yShVQ"}
